{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"ec46a67a-6fba-5bd4-9c2f-e8c6516699c9:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"tool","source":"tool_result","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a17a7ce3da74a195efcc12e1bbf0cb\",\"output\":\"Read text file `SECURITY.md`.\\n(48 line(s) above)\\n49|### Who can do what via which API\\n50|\\n51|| Interface | Who | What they can do | Guard |\\n52|| ----------- | ----- | ------------------ | ------- |\\n53|| `GET /health`, `GET /api/health` | Anyone | Check liveness (no DB) | No sensitive data returned |\\n54|| `GET /ready`, `GET /api/ready` | K8s / load-balancer | Readiness (DB check) | 503 if DB down; used as `readinessProbe` |\\n55|| `GET /metrics` | Anyone (network-restricted) | Read operational metrics | Must not leak secrets/container internals; restrict at network layer |\\n56|| `POST /webhook/gitops` | CI/CD systems | Reconcile a manifest (deploy) | `X-Signature-256` = HMAC-SHA256 of `X-Timestamp` + body (`GITOPS_WEBHOOK_TOKEN`), one signature per replay window; **fail closed** (503) if unset |\\n57|| `GET /api/v1/federation/status` | Other pilot instances | Read federation status | Constant-time federation token check; 503 without token unless `ALLOW_INSECURE_FEDERATION=true` in explicit local envs (`dev`/`development`/`local`) |\\n58|| `POST /api/v1/deployments`, `GET /api/v1/providers` | CLI / management panel (federation token holders = platform admins) | Trigger manifest reconciliation | Federation token (fail-closed by default); `user_id`+`org_id` strictly validated and checked against `manifest:deploy` for scoping/audit; `as_platform_admin=true` is asserted by the token holder (accident-prevention, not a privilege boundary — any token holder can set it); admin path is logged |\\n59|| `/api/v1/rbac/*` | Federation token holders (platform admins), scoped per-actor | Manage roles/orgs/memberships (create + revoke) | RBAC engine + per-project scoping; `actor_user_id` (query/header/body) is asserted by the token holder for scoping/audit, not independently authenticated; deletions persist via `rbac_store` (store-first, 500 without in-memory mutation on DB failure) so revokes survive restart |\\n60|| Discord app commands | Discord users | Manage VPS, backups, deploy, secrets | Bot-level role/permission checks; container names validated against `SAFE_CONTAINER_PATTERN`; health-check targets validated against allow-lists |\\n61|| `docker exec`/`docker run` (via bot) | RBAC-authorized users | Run commands in containers | **No `--privileged`, no `--cap-add=ALL`**; never `shell=True`; subprocess args passed as lists; resource limits enforced against `RESOURCE_LIMITS` |\\n62|\\n63|### Secrets and credentials\\n64|\\n65|- Secrets live in environment variables / `.env` files, **never** in code or\\n66|  committed files. Placeholders in `.env.example` are `CHANGE_ME`.\\n67|- The orchestrator **refuses to start** in production while placeholder\\n68|  secrets are set (fail fast).\\n69|- Production requires an explicit `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`; no hardcoded defaults.\\n70|- The secrets manager encrypts values at rest; keys stay out of the repo.\\n71|- Gitleaks scans the full git history on every push; npm audit and pip-audit\\n72|  run for dependency CVEs.\\n73|\\n74|### Infrastructure credentials and monitoring\\n75|\\n76|- Terraform state contains the RDS password even though it is omitted from\\n77|  outputs. The state bucket requires versioning, default SSE-S3/AES256,\\n78|  blocked public access, and restricted IAM access.\\n(more lines below)\"}","truncated":false}
